The bug arises from the incorrect handling of `ByteBuffer` instances that do not start at position 0. The original code did not account for the current position of the buffer when calculating the offset, which could lead to incorrect data being read or written, especially when the buffer's position was not at the beginning. This could result in unexpected behavior or data corruption when using the `Reader` class.

